==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|newscast|-er|id2=occupation}}.

===Noun===
{{wp}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|broadcasting|journalism}} One who [[delivers]] the [[news]] for broadcast on [[television]], [[radio]], etc; a [[newsreader]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1994|author=Rugh Winter; Bonnie Eaker-Weil|title=Adultery, the Forgivable Sin
|passage=Take Linda, a thirty-nine-year-old '''newscaster''' who relished her career but began to hear the alarm ringing on her biological clock.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1997
|author=Mervin Block
|title=Writing Broadcast News: Shorter, Sharper, Stronger
|chapter=
|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=MOykn3dMaJIC&pg=PA154
|isbn=1-56625-084-6
|page=154
|passage=Yet, a few US '''newscasters''' will go on the air at 6 pm or later and say, "Moscow said tonight.["] ... A careful writer would make his script read, "Moscow said today. ..."}}
#* {{quote-web|1=en|url=https://www.theeastafrican.co.ke/tea/oped/comment/harro-i-shrub-because-really-i-have-no-otherwise-do-i--1416060|work=w:The East African|passage=It is still considered embarrassing if people in authority like teachers or '''newscasters''' “shrub.”|title=Harro! I shrub because, really, I have no otherwise, do I?|date=2019-04-19|author=Alice Wairimu Nderitu|accessdate=2021-11-05|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230416080617/https://www.theeastafrican.co.ke/tea/oped/comment/harro-i-shrub-because-really-i-have-no-otherwise-do-i--1416060|archivedate=16 April 2023}}

